    genre: ['Fantasy', 'Horror'], subgenres: ['American'], pages: 304, chapters: 32,
    description: 'A sinister carnival arrives in a small town offering to grant wishes, in this dark fantasy about the price of desire.',
    coverColor: C[10], coverAccent: A[1], isbn: '978-1-45167-331-9', publicDomain: false, classic: true, popular: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'Something Wicked This Way Comes is Bradbury\'s most gothic novel, a dark fantasy about a carnival that preys on the desires of small-town America. Cooger and Dark\'s Pandemonium Shadow Show, with its carousel that ages and de-ages its riders, is one of fantasy\'s most memorable villains. Will and Jim, the two boys who discover the carnival\'s secret, are one of literature\'s most endearing pairs of friends. The novel\'s blend of horror, poetry, and small-town atmosphere is uniquely Bradbury.',
    whyRead: 'It is the most atmospheric fantasy ever written, a carnival of horrors that is also a poem about friendship and growing up. It is perfect October reading, and the carousel scene will give you nightmares.',
