    genre: ['Science Fiction'], subgenres: ['Political', 'American'], pages: 384, chapters: 28,
    description: 'A lunar colony revolts against Earth\'s rule, aided by a sentient computer, in this definitive novel of revolution.',
    coverColor: C[15], coverAccent: A[1], isbn: '978-0-44-178838-5', publicDomain: false, classic: true, popular: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'The Moon Is a Harsh Mistress is Heinlein\'s most political novel, a story of lunar revolution that is also a textbook on how to overthrow a government. Mike, the computer that gains consciousness and joins the revolution, is one of science fiction\'s most sympathetic AI characters. The novel\'s portrait of lunar society, with its polyamorous families and frontier justice, is one of the most detailed alternate societies in science fiction. The novel won the Hugo and is the definitive fictional account of a space revolution.',
    whyRead: 'It is the best novel about revolution in science fiction, and Mike the computer is one of the genre\'s most beloved characters. It is also a practical guide to overthrowing a government, which makes it unique.',
