    description: 'A whisky priest pursued by anti-clerical police in Mexico struggles with sin and faith in Greene\'s greatest Catholic novel.',
    coverColor: C[0], coverAccent: A[2], isbn: '978-0-14-243730-8', publicDomain: false, classic: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'The Power and the Glory is Greene\'s masterpiece, a novel about a whisky priest in revolutionary Mexico who is the last priest in his state and is hunted for his faith. The priest, a drunk and a father of a child, is the most flawed protagonist in Catholic literature, and his journey toward martyrdom is all the more powerful for his unworthiness. Greene\'s portrait of Mexico, with its heat, its poverty, and its anti-clerical violence, is one of the most atmospheric settings in twentieth-century fiction.',
