    reviewCommentary: 'The Quiet American is the most prophetic novel of the Vietnam War, written before American involvement began. Pyle, the quiet American whose idealism leads to terrorism, is one of literature\'s most devastating portraits of good intentions gone wrong. Fowler, the cynical British journalist who watches Pyle\'s destruction, is Greene\'s most sympathetic narrator. The novel\'s love triangle, with the Vietnamese woman Phuong as the prize, mirrors the political triangle of France, America, and Vietnam.',
