    description: 'A teenage gangster in Brighton murders a rival and marries a girl who knows too much, in this noir of Catholic guilt.',
    coverColor: C[2], coverAccent: A[0], isbn: '978-0-14-243730-8', publicDomain: false, classic: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'Brighton Rock is Greene\'s first great novel, a crime story that is also a theological meditation on good and evil. Pinkie, the seventeen-year-old gangster whose Catholic guilt is inseparable from his violence, is one of literature\'s most disturbing characters. Rose, the waitress he marries to keep her silent, is the novel\'s tragic heart, a girl whose love for Pinkie is a form of damnation. The novel\'s famous ending, with Rose learning what Pinkie really thought of her, is one of the most devastating in English fiction.',
    whyRead: 'It is the most intense crime novel ever written, a thriller that is also a meditation on damnation. Pinkie is one of the most chilling villains in English literature, and the ending will destroy you.',
