    description: 'A country gentleman\'s wife has an affair, and his life unravels toward one of the most shocking endings in English literature.',
    coverColor: C[6], coverAccent: A[3], isbn: '978-0-316-09425-6', publicDomain: false, classic: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'A Handful of Dust is Waugh\'s most bitter novel, a portrait of a marriage destroyed by adultery that descends into one of the most shocking endings in English fiction. Tony Last, the country gentleman who retreats to his estate while his wife Brenda has an affair in London, is one of literature\'s most sympathetic victims. The novel\'s famous ending, with Tony trapped in the Amazon reading Dickens to a madman, is the most haunting in Waugh\'s work. The title, from T.S. Eliot, signals the novel\'s descent from comedy to despair.',
