    description: 'A collection of stories including the title masterpiece, in which a family encounters the Misfit, a serial killer on a country road.',
    coverColor: C[7], coverAccent: A[0], isbn: '978-0-15-636465-2', publicDomain: false, classic: true, popular: true, trending: true,
    reviewCommentary: 'A Good Man Is Hard to Find is the greatest collection of short stories in American literature, and its title story, in which a grandmother and her family are murdered by the Misfit on a deserted road, is the most perfect short story ever written. O\'Connor\'s vision of the South, where grace arrives through violence and where religious faith is inseparable from brutality, is unique in American fiction. The Misfit, who concludes that there is no pleasure in life but meanness, is one of literature\'s most terrifying philosophers.',
